menu "strres: user-visible strings on a filesystem"

    config STRRES_CACHE_SECTIONS
        int "Cached sections"
        default 3
        range 1 16
        help
            How many string sections are kept in memory at once, over and above
            the pinned section, which is always resident.

            Each slot holds one whole section file in one allocation -- a few
            kilobytes -- so this is the component's main memory cost. A section
            is roughly one command group, and printing that group's help touches
            it once, so even 1 works; 3 keeps a couple of neighbouring groups
            warm without measurable cost.

            Nothing grows past this: a lookup that would need a slot while every
            slot is held fails and prints its id, rather than allocating.

    config STRRES_FORMAT_BUF_SIZE
        int "Format buffer for strres_error(), bytes"
        default 256
        range 64 1024
        help
            diag has no verror(), so an error string is formatted here before
            being emitted in one call -- splitting the "ERR: " prefix from the
            text would let another task's line land between them.

            On the stack of the calling task, not static. A longer message is
            truncated, not split.

    config STRRES_BASE_DIR
        string "Directory holding the locale subdirectories"
        default "/res/str"
        help
            One subdirectory per locale beneath this, each holding the .sr files
            for that language. The application mounts the filesystem; this
            component only opens paths under it.

    config STRRES_DEFAULT_LOCALE
        string "Default locale"
        default "en-US"
        help
            Used when none is configured, and as the fallback when the requested
            locale has no files on the partition.

    config STRRES_DEBUG_NAMES
        bool "Name missing strings instead of numbering them"
        default n
        help
            A string that cannot be found normally prints as "[str:04F2]",
            because a table mapping ids to names would put strings back into the
            image -- which is what this component exists to avoid. Decode one
            with the strres_ids.txt the build emits.

            Turning this on emits that table anyway and prints
            "[str:i2c/scan.help]" directly. Convenient while migrating strings,
            and worth several kilobytes of flash, so leave it off in a release.

endmenu
